  "title": "Erdős Problem #997",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Call $x_1,x_2,\\ldots \\in (0,1)$ well-distributed if, for every $\\epsilon>0$, if $k$ is sufficiently large then, for all $n>0$ and intervals $I\\subseteq [0,1]$, $ \\lvert \\# \\{ n<m\\leq n+k : x_m\\in I\\} - \\lvert I\\rvert k\\rvert < \\epsilon k. $ Is it true that, for every $\\alpha$, the sequence $\\{ \\alpha p_n\\}$ is not well-distributed, if $p_n$ is the sequence of primes?",
